.TH LX 1 "August 2026" "lx 0.1.0" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
lx \- power your Linux experience: system info, network, processes, packages, tuning, security, cleanup, services, backups, health
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B lx
[\fIOPTIONS\fR] \fICOMMAND\fR [\fIARGS\fR]...
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B lx
is a modern, feature-rich CLI toolkit that bundles dozens of system
inspection, network, process, package, tweak, security, cleanup, and
service utilities behind a single colorful command.
.PP
Run
.B lx --help
for the command list and
.B lx COMMAND --help
for details on a specific command.
.SH COMMANDS
.TP
.B info
Show system information: OS, kernel, CPU, memory, disk, GPU, network, uptime.
Flags: \fB--cpu\fR, \fB--mem\fR, \fB--disk\fR, \fB--gpu\fR, \fB--net\fR.
.TP
.B net
Network tools: \fBiface\fR (interfaces), \fBports\fR (listening sockets),
\fBip\fR (public IP), \fBspeed\fR (download speed test), \fBtrace\fR HOST
(traceroute), \fBall\fR.
.TP
.B proc
Process manager: \fBtop\fR [-n NUM] [-s cpu|mem|rss|time], \fBfind\fR NAME,
\fBtree\fR [NAME], \fBkill\fR [-9] PATTERN, \fBme\fR.
.TP
.B pkg
Unified package manager wrapper for apt/dnf/pacman/zypper/apk/flatpak/snap:
\fBstatus\fR, \fBsearch\fR QUERY, \fBupdate\fR, \fBupgrade\fR, \fBinstall\fR
NAME, \fBremove\fR NAME, \fBpurge\fR. Backend auto-detected, override with
\fB-b/--backend\fR.
.TP
.B tweak
System tuning. \fBshow\fR, \fBswappiness\fR N [--no-persist], \fBmax-files\fR N,
\fBgovernor\fR NAME, \fBbbr\fR, \fBinteractive\fR, \fBset\fR KEY VALUE.
Most tweak subcommands require root.
.TP
.B sec
Security audit. \fBaudit\fR [--no-suid], \fBssh\fR, \fBports\fR, \fBsuid\fR,
\fBhardssh\fR (writes hardening drop-in).
.TP
.B clean
Free disk space. \fBcache\fR, \fBlogs\fR [--vacuum MB], \fBkernels\fR
[--keep N], \fBreport\fR. Destructive subcommands require root and confirm.
.TP
.B service
systemd wrapper: \fBstatus\fR NAME, \fBlist\fR [--state S] [--type T],
\fBfailed\fR, \fBlog\fR NAME, \fBstart\fR/\fBstop\fR/\fBrestart\fR NAME,
\fBenable\fR/\fBdisable\fR NAME, \fBtimers\fR.
.TP
.B backup
Dotfile & config backup. \fBcreate\fR [-d DEST] [-t EXTRA], \fBlist\fR,
\fBrestore\fR ARCHIVE [--dry-run].
.TP
.B health
Compute an overall system health score (0-100) from CPU load, memory,
disk, swap, temperature, uptime, failed units, and zombies.
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.B \-\-version
Print version and exit.
.TP
.B \-h, \-\-help
Show help and exit.
.SH EXAMPLES
.TP
Snapshot the system:
.B lx info
.TP
Show listening ports:
.B lx net ports -a
.TP
Top 20 processes by memory:
.B lx proc top -n 20 -s mem
.TP
Upgrade all packages (auto-detects apt on Debian/Ubuntu):
.B lx pkg upgrade -y
.TP
Apply desktop-friendly tuning (requires root):
.B sudo lx tweak interactive
.TP
Full security audit:
.B lx sec audit
.TP
Free up old kernels, keeping the newest 2 (requires root):
.B sudo lx clean kernels --keep 2 -y
.TP
Back up dotfiles:
.B lx backup create
.SH FILES
.TP
.I /etc/sysctl.d/90-lx.conf
Persistent sysctl settings written by
.B lx tweak
commands (when \fB--persist\fR, the default).
.TP
.I /etc/security/limits.conf
Updated by
.B lx tweak max-files
.TP
.I /etc/ssh/sshd_config.d/99-lx-hardening.conf
Hardening drop-in written by
.B lx sec hardssh
.TP
.I ~/lx-backups/
Default destination for
.B lx backup create
.SH EXIT STATUS
Returns 0 on success, 1 on runtime errors, 2 on CLI usage errors, 130 on
interrupt, and 124 if a subprocess times out.
.SH BUGS
Report issues via your distribution's bug tracker or the project's issue
tracker. Include the output of \fBlx --version\fR and the failing command.
